course: dictionary
lesson: 10506
title: Twiddle: twist it, or wait with nothing to do
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To twiddle means to twist, turn or play with something with your fingers, often without thinking. You can twiddle a knob, a pencil or a strand of your hair. It is a small, fidgety movement.
explain: Twiddle also appears in the phrase «twiddle your thumbs», which means to sit doing nothing while you wait, feeling bored. The words around it tell you which meaning is right: is someone's hand busy with an object, or are they just waiting?
explain: In the example text, «a twiddle for E» is a little twisting curl used as a sign in a picture of the alphabet. Notice how the words «for E» tell you which kind of twiddle is meant. Use the context to check your meaning, then swap it into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Twiddle can be a verb (you twiddle something) or a noun (you make a twiddle).
fact: «Twiddle» means to twist, turn or play with something with your fingers.
fact: «Twiddle your thumbs» means to sit doing nothing, waiting and bored.
fact: The verb changes its form: twiddles, twiddled, twiddling. «She twiddled her pencil while she waited.»
fact: In the alphabet picture, «a twiddle for E» is a little twisting curl, one of the signs used in the pictures.
exercise: «She twiddled the dial until the music came in clearly.» What does twiddled mean here? | Sat and did nothing | Shouted at it | Threw it across the room | *Turned and twisted, with her fingers
exercise: «We had to twiddle our thumbs for an hour while the bus was late.» What does twiddle our thumbs mean? | Ran to catch the bus | Clapped our hands together | *Sat doing nothing, bored and waiting | Played a fast game
exercise: In the alphabet picture, «a twiddle for E» is which kind of thing? | A loud noise | A kind of animal | A long river | *A little twisty curl
test: Which word in «make a twiddle for E, beavers for B» names something that is not a letter? | *beavers | make | for | twiddle
test: Ben says, «Stop twiddling your hair, you're making me dizzy!» What does Ben mean? | *Please stop twisting your hair with your fingers | Please cut your hair short | Please sing louder | Please dance around the room
exam: Which sentence uses twiddle to mean sitting and waiting with nothing to do? | «We twiddled the knob to make the light brighter.» | *«We had to twiddle our thumbs in the queue for ages.» | «The twiddle on the sign was small and curly.» | «She twiddled her pen and wrote her name.»
